cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "TAL - Theory-Adaptive Learning: Compositional Symbolic Regression with Adaptive Grammar Selection"
version: 4.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
license: MIT
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fenech-Casoni"
    given-names: ""
abstract: >
  TAL is a compositional symbolic regression framework that adaptively
  selects between two grammars (base: 8 operators; extended: 13 operators)
  and uses a multi-start parametric fitter with parametric memory to
  recover closed-form expressions from data. The framework is evaluated
  on 17 benchmark functions spanning four domains: Feynman equations,
  ordinary differential equations, dynamical systems, and empirical
  functions.
keywords:
  - symbolic regression
  - equation discovery
  - genetic programming
  - grammar-based search
  - scientific machine learning
repository-code: "https://github.com/fenech-casoni/tal"
